<element name="TCDDrawerCommon.DrawFocusRect">
<short>
Draws a focus rectangle on the specified canvas.
</short>
<descr>
<p>
<var>DrawFocusRect</var> is an overridden method in 
<var>TCDDrawerCommon</var>. It implements the abstract virtual method 
introduced in the <var>TCustomDrawer</var> ancestor. It is used to draw a 
focus rectangle to the canvas specified in <var>ADest</var>. 
</p>
<p>
<var>ADestPos</var> is a <var>TPoint</var> instance which contains the canvas 
coordinates (in the X and Y members) for the top-left corner of the focus 
rectangle. 
</p>
<p>
<var>ASize</var> is a <var>TSize</var> instance which contains the width and 
height (in the CX and CY members) for the focus rectangle.
</p>
<p>
In TCDDrawerCommon, DrawFocusRect draws the focus rectangle as a dotted black 
line on a white background. Other areas on ADest are not affected in the 
method.
</p>
</descr>
<seealso>
</seealso>
</element>
<element name="TCDDrawerCommon.DrawFocusRect.ADest">
<short>
Canvas where the focus rectangle is drawn.
</short>
</element>
<element name="TCDDrawerCommon.DrawFocusRect.ADestPos">
<short>
Position where the top-left corner of the focus rectangle is located on the 
canvas.
</short>
</element>
<element name="TCDDrawerCommon.DrawFocusRect.ASize">
<short>
Contains the width and height for the focus rectangle.
</short>
</element>

